<div class="card list" style="width: 95%; max-width: 45rem;">
   <div class="card-body listHeader">
      <h3 class="font-weight-bold mb-0">Privacy Policy</h3>
      <p class="mb-0">Effective {{effectiveDate}}</p>
   </div>
   <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
      <li class="list-group-item">
         <p>Lori's List is a shared shopping list service run by Zachary Horine ("we", "us"). This policy covers the website at lorislist.horinetech.com and the Lori's List apps for iPhone, iPad and Android. In short: we keep only what the service needs to work, we never sell it, and we don't use it for advertising or tracking.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="list-group-item">
         <h4>What we collect</h4>
         <ul>
            <li><b>Account details:</b> your first and last name, username, email address, and your password. Passwords are stored only as a one-way hash, so nobody, including us, can read them.</li>
            <li><b>Your lists:</b> list names and colors, the items on them, quantities, and whether items are checked off.</li>
            <li><b>Sharing:</b> who you share a list with, the email address you sent an invitation to, and whether each person can edit or only view.</li>
            <li><b>Signed-in devices:</b> for each device signed in to the apps, a device name, when it signed in and when it was last used. These are shown to you under "Signed-in devices" so you can sign a device out.</li>
            <li><b>Technical information:</b> your IP address is used briefly to protect sign-in and password reset from abuse, and our server keeps standard access and error logs.</li>
         </ul>
         <p>We don't collect your location, contacts, photos, advertising identifiers, or payment information, and the apps contain no analytics or advertising code.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="list-group-item">
         <h4>How we use it</h4>
         <p>Only to run Lori's List: to sign you in, store and sync your lists across your devices, let the people you share with see them, send the emails you ask for (password resets and list invitations), keep the service secure, and answer you when you contact us.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="list-group-item">
         <h4>Who can see it</h4>
         <ul>
            <li><b>People you share a list with</b> can see that list, its items, and your name as its owner.</li>
            <li><b>Service providers:</b> our emails are delivered through an email provider, which handles the recipient's address and the message. The website loads fonts and styles from Google Fonts, Font Awesome and cdnjs, which see your IP address when your browser fetches them.</li>
            <li><b>The law:</b> we will disclose information if a valid legal request requires it.</li>
         </ul>
         <p>We don't sell, rent or trade your information.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="list-group-item">
         <h4>Cookies and storage on your device</h4>
         <p>The website uses one cookie to keep you signed in. The apps keep their sign-in in your device's secure storage (the Keychain on Apple devices), and keep a copy of your lists on the device so they work offline. Signing out or deleting the app removes them.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="list-group-item">
         <h4>How long we keep it</h4>
         <p>We keep your account and lists until you delete them or your account. Deleted lists and items are removed from the database. Device sign-ins expire on their own if unused, and server logs are kept only as long as needed for security and troubleshooting.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="list-group-item">
         <h4>Your choices</h4>
         <ul>
            <li>You can see and change your name, email and password under My Account, and delete any list you own.</li>
            <li>You can sign any device out under "Signed-in devices".</li>
            <li>To delete your account, choose Delete account under My Account on the website or in the app, and enter your password. This immediately deletes your account, the lists you own (with their items and shares), your item suggestions, pending invitations and every device sign-in. Lists other people shared with you stay with their owners, as do items you added to them. Your username can't be registered again. If you can't sign in, email <a href="mailto:admin@horine.dev">admin@horine.dev</a> from the address on your account and we will delete it for you.</li>
            <li>You can ask us for a copy of your information, or to correct it, at the same address.</li>
         </ul>
      </li>
      <li class="list-group-item">
         <h4>Security</h4>
         <p>All traffic to Lori's List is encrypted with HTTPS, passwords and sign-in tokens are stored only as hashes, and you can sign out every device at once. No system is perfectly secure, but we work to keep your information safe.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="list-group-item">
         <h4>Children</h4>
         <p>Lori's List is not directed to children under 13, and we don't knowingly collect information from them. If you believe a child has made an account, contact us and we will delete it.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="list-group-item">
         <h4>Changes</h4>
         <p>If we change this policy we will update it here and change the date at the top. For significant changes we will let account holders know by email or in the app.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="list-group-item">
         <h4>Contact</h4>
         <p>Questions about privacy: <a href="mailto:admin@horine.dev">admin@horine.dev</a>. See also our <a href="/terms">Terms of Use</a>.</p>
      </li>
   </ul>
</div>
